@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 19 and 20"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch19ch20_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-12): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's instruction 2026-11-12 ('OK, let's proceed with Chapters 19 and 20, the same ceremonies').
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the latest version of every lineage file was read; ordinals 3 to 7 are taken in the narrow-lineage files and 1 to 4 in the slides register (different namespace); the next free ordinal is 8. Lineage8 (ch17-18) was closed LS_Achieved on 2026-11-12 with its closure report, owner-confirmed (commit 1ff01d8), before this lineage opened. Lineage3 (ch9-10) is still open with one carried-forward item (TK_Ret_Ch09_Research/_Verify), a pre-existing state not changed here and reported to the owner.
STATE-CHECK PRECEDING THIS OPENING (live files measured 2026-11-12, not memory and not the 2026-10-25 logs): chapters 19 (Keeping Time, Scheduling Tasks and Launching Programs) and 20 (Sending Email, Texts and Push Notifications) never received the iteration-20 retrofit that chapters 9 to 18 received. Chapter 19: deck sen0414_ch19_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (26 slides, in 08-tooling/ch19-deck, none in 03-materials/ch19), page v9_34_0, no chapter-code manifest, stories script v1_0_0 (6 stories, self-check clean, no story link shared with chapters 1 to 18; the name Bell Labs occurs in chapters 5, 8 and 19 and is to be examined). Chapter 20: deck v1_0_1 (26 slides, same place), page v9_35_0, no manifest, stories script v1_0_0 (6 stories, self-check clean, no shared link). The deck standard check v1.0.0 fails 7 of 13 for both decks (D1 slide 1 unnumbered; D2 text boxes over 30 words, 28 in chapter 19 and 42 in chapter 20; D3 code slides without a visual result; D4 no everyday analogy for any of 36 and 34 concepts; D5 story slides lack a picture and the full 5N1K; D7 speaker notes over 60 words on all 26 slides; D11 research coverage 38.9 percent and 61.8 percent) and does not measure D10 and M1; the overlap check is clean for both. The research checks of both chapters fail at their execution step (chapter 19 rdodi_data v1_0_6, chapter 20 v1_0_2). The register of the closed slides lineage records the retrofit tasks of both chapters (TK_Ret_Ch19_* and TK_Ret_Ch20_*) as Ready, never done there. The rdodi/ research-artifact folders exist for both chapters and are out of scope, as in Lineage6 and Lineage8."""@en .

ex:ProfileDecl8 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 to Lineage7: work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work. Level L2 stated plainly." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-19"^^xsd:date .

ex:Lineage8 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 19 and 20, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission8 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 8 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl8 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage7 do; chapters 19 and 20's retrofit tasks stayed Ready there."@en .

ex:Mission8 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 19 and 20 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog8 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 19 (Keeping Time, Scheduling Tasks and Launching Programs) and 20 (Sending Email, Texts and Push Notifications) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft and built to the deck and page standards that chapters 9 to 18 meet: a true, sourced story per concept the chapter teaches, none repeated from the chapters already presented, an accurate resources slide, and any open item named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction 2026-11-12, following the Lineage3 to Lineage7 pattern and their stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages." .
